{"skill":{"slug":"ai-web-automation","displayName":"AI Web Automation"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1771571108805,"changelog":"Initial release","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":948,"sha256":"372e572615e61b149f679c01cb21f1ea8d0588e8b8854b07a706875d160e463d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"main.py","size":1905,"sha256":"7f528d931e71ffa2c6879b448680c6065c5368ac4d968afd18d74a7f2ce2d13d","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"package.json","size":525,"sha256":"dce79ccd9aaac4eab90d706bb225c31c421d256c2a341711ad840e3733345e27","contentType":"application/json"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789074654672,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"07df86e683c751bd390ea74094ff75729c45aa2ecce61af97cdaf5237475ab73","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/07df86e683c751bd390ea74094ff75729c45aa2ecce61af97cdaf5237475ab73","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: ai-web-automation\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is classified as suspicious due to a Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) vulnerability in `main.py`. The script directly uses user-provided URLs from `sys.argv` in `requests.get()` without validation, potentially allowing an attacker to force the agent to make requests to internal network resources or sensitive endpoints. While the `SKILL.md` describes high-risk capabilities like scheduled tasks and proxy support, the immediate and concrete vulnerability lies in the `main.py`'s handling of the `url` parameter for web scraping.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779165623109},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":17,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789074654672},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"The skill is a simple web-scraping tool, but it can fetch arbitrary user-supplied URLs without destination limits, which could expose local or internal network services if misused.","dimensions":[{"detail":"main.py accepts an arbitrary URL and calls requests.get with redirects enabled and no scheme, host, IP range, port, or redirect validation; that is broader network reach than a safely scoped scraper needs.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No install script, dependency installation, remote payload retrieval, or tool replacement behavior was found in the inspected package metadata.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions advertise scraping, scheduled tasks, automated submissions, proxy pool support, and notifications without documented authorization, rate-limit, robots/ToS, privacy, or confirmation guardrails.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The code creates an artifact/output report directory and writes scrape reports, but no cross-session service, scheduled task, privilege escalation, memory modification, or background persistence was found in code.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is web automation and scraping; the actual runtime implementation only supports a scrape action that fetches a URL, extracts limited page metadata, and writes a local Markdown report.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with the skill making outbound web requests from your agent environment. Use it only for authorized targets, avoid internal/private/metadata URLs, and review or add URL allowlisting, redirect validation, rate limits, and confirmation for any future scheduled, proxy, or submission features.","findings":"[T09] unexpected: The scanner's SSRF concern is supported by artifact evidence: user-controlled input is passed directly to requests.get, allowing loopback, private-network, metadata, or redirect targets to be requested from the runtime network context. This is a Review concern, not evidence of malicious intent.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The broad web automation features are advertised without safety scoping. Some advertised capabilities are not implemented in the current code, which downgrades impact, but the lack of documented guardrails remains relevant for users evaluating the skill.\n[SQP-3] expected: Chinese-language documentation and comments are present. This is a usability/localization note rather than a security concern, and it did not drive the verdict.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789074654672}}}}}